    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The delayed diagnosis of breast cancer in Africa is a significant public health challenge, with women often waiting  more than six months  after noticing symptoms. This delay is often attributed inefficiencies in the healthcare system and limited access to specialized care, resulting in  more than half  of African women receiving a late-stage diagnosis. Unfortunately, a late diagnosis reduces survival chances and increases the cost of cancer care due to expensive therapies and longer hospital stays.",
